{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an integer array `nums`, return the **maximum difference between two successive elements in its sorted form**. Return 0 if there are fewer than two elements. You must solve it in **linear time and linear space**."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/be697906-a594-43f8-82fc-92ef0a7351f9.svg",
      "alt": "The values 1, 5, 10, 25, 50 and 52 on a number line from 1 to 52. There are 5 gaps covering a distance of 51, so the biggest gap is at least 51 divided by 5, about 10. Buckets of width 10 are drawn: any two values in the same bucket are less than 10 apart, so the biggest gap must run from one bucket's maximum to a later bucket's minimum — here from 25 to 50, a gap of 25.",
      "width": 844,
      "height": 305,
